NNAAMMEE
     wwllaann__ttkkiipp — TKIP and Michael crypto support for 802.11 devices

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     ddeevviiccee wwllaann__ttkkiipp

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The wwllaann__ttkkiipp module handles the TKIP and Michael cryptographic require‐
     ments of the WPA and 802.11i protocols.  It does encapsulation and decap‐
     sulation of TKIP-encoded 802.11 frames and optionally calculates the TKIP
     cipher and Michael MIC.  The wwllaann__ttkkiipp module is an 802.11 cryptographic
     plugin module for use by the wlan(4) module.  This module is automati‐
     cally loaded if a TKIP key is configured; typically by a WPA supplicant
     program such as wpa_supplicant, or a WPA authenticator program such as
     hhoossttaappdd.  Should the underlying network device not be capable of doing
     the TKIP and/or Michael calculations in hardware, the wwllaann__ttkkiipp module
     will do the work.

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     wlan(4), wlan_ccmp(4), wlan_wep(4)

SSTTAANNDDAARRDDSS
     More information can be found in the IEEE 802.11, WPA, and 802.11i Stan‐
     dards.

HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The wwllaann__ttkkiipp driver first appeared in FreeBSD 6.0.

